Z||000000||Greg Piet||09-10-2000||01:44 AM||||Well i was compelled to get a toy that wasnt directly bolted onto my Fiero...   So I got a cell...  <BR>Sprint PCS service as you might have guessed.<BR>I tried to activate the thing, got disconnected in the middle of it, called back on a normal phone to finish it, then I had to call 3 other times to get the thing activated.<BR>WHAT A PAIN!!!!!!!<BR>They kept telling me I was activated, and I kept telling them my little phone was not working....<BR>Their answer was wait 2 hours,   then wait 10 to 16 hours , then wait 8 more hours...<BR>The last time it was up in 5 minutes....<BR>Whats up with that????<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||TOM||09-10-2000||01:53 AM||||Het greg I will be in vegas the last weekend in sept. Wanna chat?||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||09-10-2000||03:28 AM||||I use Sprint for my digital phone as well. Had the EXACT same prob. when I first had it activated. They also have pretty crappy coverage here to. Memphis covers some 400+ square miles, and I swear they have one tower covering the whole city! Oh well, I usually dont have too much of a prob. though...I guess its alright.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ozzy||09-10-2000||09:23 PM||||Sprint PCS sucks big time dude...I have had their service for awhile now. If you change service plans, I promise they will never get your bill right again! The phones work great when you are in their coverage area but it is so limited to cities and major interstate corridoors that it is not a practical roaming phone. The analogue service available on the dual band phones will cost you both arms and both legs.<P><BR>Ozzy||||reg||13
Z||000004||Monkeyman||09-10-2000||09:54 PM||||I thought about getting cell phone service, but since my credit is less than perfect, they wanted a $600US deposit.  **** you very much, but no thanx.  It's easier to get a mortgage for a house than to get cell service.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||09-11-2000||03:21 AM||||Well i signed one of those year long thingys and got a "free" option.<BR>I chose the free 50 minutes of roaming, and yes I have a motorola dual band phone so I figure it should work if I really need it most places.<P>So far people say it is really clear, especially compared to the older analog stuff<P>P.S. Tom I emailed you at your hotmail acct.<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 09-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||09-12-2000||10:57 AM||||When it works, it works pretty darn good.  When it doesent, the phone is a paperweight.  The thing I like about Sprint is that it is the first new voice network in a long time.  <P>New services like Verizon (formerly Primeco) and Sprint PCS are using the latest technology, so it will take years to get the entire country covered.  It took the original cellular compaines 10 years to do it.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000007||olympic||09-12-2000||12:30 PM||||   The cellular system in the US sucks!!   Those roaming charges are outrageous.  They even charge you just for having the phone turned on!  Here in Canada I can take my cell phone anywhere in the country with zero roaming charges.  My long distance and airtime charges never change even if I'm out of my province.  <P>  Basically the telephone companies got together and agreed to do this to increase business.  The US should do this as well but they have way more telephone companies that would have to agree.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||09-12-2000||01:26 PM||||Maybe it is different here in the States, but I have never been hit with a roaming charge unless I was "roaming" and talking on my phone. The last year and a half my phone has been on quite a few cross country trips, always turned on, and never charged for roaming, unless a call is placed.<P>I've been with AirTouch(now Verizon)for the last 3 years. Couple months ago, I ditched my 3 year old analog phone, for a new digital one. The calls on my digital are exactly the same as my analog. Nobody would believe me I was talking on a cell phone until they tried it out, can't tell a difference. Plus, the only place I have ever found I couldn't use my phone, was way out in BFE out in Indiana.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Greg Piet||09-12-2000||04:38 PM||||From what I understand I am not charged with roaming stuff unless I am talking.  My father had one of the original cellphones that took up a briefcase and that one he was charged if it was on and he hopped from one cell site to another, but I think that is gone for the most part now.<BR>A even inquired to a friend who has had service for a year now and he told me that I did not get charged roaming unless I am placing or getting a call and I answer it.<P>So...  if I am not in PCS land I just do not answer it and read the message it leaves or use the caller ID.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Phil||09-12-2000||07:18 PM||||We just got the Verizon no raoming or long distance charges anywhere in the US.  150 min for $39/mo. We only use our phone while traveling anyway so this is working out quite well. So far we have found that as long as anybody else can get their phone to connect so can we, so coverage seems to be nation wide.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Ozzy||09-12-2000||08:30 PM||||I don't think olympic meant that anyone will be charged for carrying an activated phone into a roaming area.(?) I dont think that would be legal! <P>I must agree somewhat; the cell system and companies are very complicated here. Before I left Australia, calling party pays!!! You do not get charged airtime for incoming calls. Made complete sense to me. The billing systems here are sophisticated enough to handle that but the cell companies won't hear of it. Also no roaming charges. I don't wish to whine about the U.S. as it has been very good to me. I do think the cell services could use some streamlining though.<P>Ozzy||||reg||10
Z||000012||whamel||09-13-2000||10:56 AM||||I had to go with Nextel - Sprint PCS couldn't cover my area.  I have been darn happy with it since I got it.  Free incoming calls - free long distance and all that fun stuff.  It's a bit more expensive, but I've been all over the country with it and I only seem to lose signal on those trips through PA in the serious mountains.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Cliff Pennock||09-13-2000||12:45 PM||||Mobile phones are very common here in Holland and extremely cheap. There's even a supermarket-chain that gives them away whenever your total groceries exceeds $10 (yes, *ten* dollars).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Songman||09-13-2000||11:32 PM||||I have a Cricket phone for here in Nashville. Their advertisement says all the local calls you want for only $29 per month.. Of course, after you add voice mail, call waiting, caller ID, tax, etc... My bill comes to just over $40. Not too bad really but the coverage sucks! It will not work in my house but if I go stand it my front yard it will work - sometimes....<P>I guess I got spoiled by my Sprint PCS phone that was great and worked almost everywhere... but it was costing me $400 per month! Now I have this nice $200 Sprint PCS paper weight lying her on my desk.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Greg Piet||09-14-2000||02:01 PM||||400 dollars?   I am only spending 30 a month, I suppose you are a lot more popular than I am!||||reg||1
Z||000016||LarryB||09-14-2000||03:41 PM||||Everybody in Field Operations where I work (over 200 of us throughout the US) got switched over to Sprint PCS from Nextel a few months ago (even if we're not techs and not on any on-call list we still get phones).  Not that Nextel was that great, but the only place I've been where Sprint's coverage didn't suck rocks was Manhattan. We're trying to get the corporate bozos to switch us to something else.  <P>Before we all got Nextels I had Bell Atlantic Mobile for business phone.  That was better than either Nextel or Sprint.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Raydar||09-15-2000||09:23 AM||||Don't know how long this link will remain active. The writer describes Sprint's customer service, or lack thereof... <A HREF="http://www.dallasobserver.com/issues/2000-09-14/news.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.dallasobserver.com/issues/2000-09-14/news.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000018||bHooper||09-15-2000||10:43 AM||||I have had Verizon (formerly GTE, formerly Cell one) for 7 years, and 3 phones, and am very happy.<P>I just got my 3rd phone yesterday, a Qualcomm 860... buy 2 for $9.99!  With a 1 year contact.  So I got one for my girlfriend and one for me.<P>The service plan that I am on now is $35 for 300 min with no roaming or longdistance in NC!  Not bad.  Plus they throw in 3 months of "internet" access for the phone.<P>This works well for me because I have one friend that works in the "repair shop" (read: no charge for cig plugs, spare batt. or leather case  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) and one friend that works on the switch's (read: my house is well covered with service)<P>Having friends work for a utility is a complete blessing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
